WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.540
Speaker 1: Facebook has decided to uphold
the ban on Donald Trump and will reassess

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.180
the decision in a few months.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:11.820
This was a decision we knew had been made
a couple of days ago by Facebook's oversight

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:16.650
board, and it was set to be announced this
morning at nine a.m. and as promised, that

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.280
right around 9:00 a.m.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:24.570
Eastern, the company's decision to suspend
Donald Trump on both Facebook and Instagram

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:29.610
was confirmed and extended for at least a
period of several months.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:34.920
The board did rule that an indefinite suspension
of Trump was not appropriate.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.679
So that time frame has now been amended.

00:00:38.679 --> 00:00:45.570
And the board said that they are going to
rereview this at some period of time in the

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.359
relative future.

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:51.760
It seems as though it will happen within six
months.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.719
The board asked that Facebook complete the
review within six months and said that maybe

00:00:57.719 --> 00:01:03.639
some clear policies could be made to balance
public safety and freedom of expression.

00:01:03.639 --> 00:01:08.710
Remember that originally the ban on Donald
Trump from Facebook different than the one

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:09.710
on Twitter.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:15.640
I mean, every platform had their sort of own
justification was that the risk to public

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:25.550
safety exceeded Facebook's purported desire
to allow freedom of expression.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:32.650
And they made that decision shortly after
the January 6th Trump riot insurrection of

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.490
the US capital.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:39.110
This was the most aggressive action Facebook
had taken against Trump during his entire

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.540
four year term.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:45.410
And Mark Zuckerberg, the Facebook CEO, said
at the time, quote, We believe the risks of

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:50.020
allowing the president to continue to use
our service during this period are simply

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.700
too great.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:57.550
That decision was then referred to the oversight
board several weeks later because it was such

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.840
a significant decision.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:04.890
They wanted the board to review it and independently
judge whether Trump should remain banned.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:09.759
And now, indeed, they are saying it will be
I mean, I guess we're saying at least six

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:12.410
months and then it will be reviewed again.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:17.849
So depending on how you want to interpret
this news, it Trump continues banned and it's

00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:21.840
a sledgehammer and cudgel against the free
speech of a former president.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.040
That's the way the right is reacting.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.760
And we'll have some of those reaction clips
maybe tomorrow, depending on what else is

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:28.760
going on.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:29.760
Maybe not.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:35.299
On the other hand, the news seems to be signaling
that at some point Trump is coming back.

00:02:35.299 --> 00:02:40.189
And my prediction would be that if it's in
six months or five or seven or whatever, at

00:02:40.189 --> 00:02:47.139
a certain point the oversight board at Facebook
will determine that at this time, because

00:02:47.139 --> 00:02:54.389
things have simmer down or whatever the case
may be at that time, the impetus for providing

00:02:54.389 --> 00:03:00.290
a platform for expression to a former president
will override in this kind of balancing act

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.599
the risk to public safety.

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:05.389
There will still be a risk to public safety
of allowing Trump back on Facebook, but it

00:03:05.389 --> 00:03:08.500
will be overridden given the circumstances
at the time.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:15.180
Now, even though this is the news here is
they have decided the ban is no longer indefinite.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.260
They've announced it is no longer a permanent
ban.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.650
Fox News couldn't even get the story correct.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:26.029
Fox News went to air this morning with a story
called Facebook Oversight Board Bans Trump

00:03:26.029 --> 00:03:27.029
for life.

00:03:27.029 --> 00:03:28.610
That's just inaccurate.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:29.790
It's the opposite of the decision.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:35.739
I mean, I guess if you think Trump won't live
six months, I guess in a sense Trump may be

00:03:35.739 --> 00:03:39.670
banned for his life, but that is not the story.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:47.120
Now, it's obvious that if allowed back on
the platform, Donald Trump would immediately

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:55.439
resume using the platform to spread corrosive
lies and weaponized disinformation.

00:03:55.439 --> 00:04:03.260
The only question is whether he should be
allowed to do some of that, because there

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:10.400
should be emphasis placed on allowing a former
president to use these platforms to communicate,

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.940
even in a situation where someone else, a
sort of mere mortal, so to speak, you know,

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.910
a civilian, a normal person, would not be
allowed to do that.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:25.970
And that's a question that the Facebook board
will answer, presumably in about six months.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:34.030
Now, in terms of what we're going to get later,
actually, to Donald Trump's desire to communicate

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:41.220
directly with the public, he has launched
now this much promoted new communication platform.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.220
It's just a.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:47.060
Log and we're going to get to that later,
but there is no question that, you know, six

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:52.390
months from now we will be well into the twenty,
twenty two campaign.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:57.580
I know it sounds insane because Trump still
hasn't accepted the results of twenty twenty.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:01.080
Trump still hasn't even accepted the popular
vote results of 2016.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:07.260
But six months from now, we will be under
a year out from the midterms.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:13.000
And so Trump's desire to play kingmaker and
to determine who is a real Republican, as

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.680
far as he's concerned, that is going to be
riding very high in six months, which will

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.280
be early November of twenty twenty one.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.250
So there's no question that we're going to
be hearing more from Trump by then one way

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.250
or another.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:24.820
The question is whether we will be hearing
from him on Facebook.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:30.120
For now, Trump remains banned, but it is no
longer an indefinite ban and we'll have more

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.140
on that as needed.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.520
Maybe tomorrow or maybe not

